WEBVTT

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:41.840
Are you awake?

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.460
Yeah, where are we now?

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:50.520
We'll arrive at Ohtsu soon and enter
the Hanshin Highway within an hour.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.860
Surprisingly, you drive quite slowly.

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.850
We can cover long distances faster this way.

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.300
It would be different if we were cruising at 200km/h.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:03.350
But the speed difference would be offset
if we took five minute breaks between.

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:08.350
So you like long-distance cruises?

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.280
I like it and sometimes I go around aimlessly.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.530
When I'm not driving around other cars,

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.130
I feel as if I can clearly hear the sounds of the engine,

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:22.120
which are normally absorbed by the sounds of the exhaust.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.580
You really like cars, huh?

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:28.800
No, I don't, I just like to drive.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:32.410
That's wrong. To you, it actually doesn't mater if you drive or not.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.640
What do you mean?

00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:38.470
Trying to modify something on a car, going for a drive...

00:02:38.470 --> 00:02:42.140
You're not the kind of person who
would do such a thing with a car...

00:02:42.810 --> 00:02:44.520
You like the car itself.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:50.150
Which car do you like the most? BlackBird? Or...

00:02:53.950 --> 00:02:59.780
<i>Osaka Midnight</i>

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:23.810
Maki, that's all for today.

00:03:23.810 --> 00:03:27.070
Get down from a ramp nearby on the highway and go home.

00:03:27.070 --> 00:03:29.060
Wait a moment, brother, there's still...

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:33.000
You still haven't fully understood your car.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:34.570
If you get too excited, you'll just get into an accident.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.650
What about you, brother?

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:41.570
I'll drive a bit more, a guest is coming from Tokyo.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.080
Guest?

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:47.290
Yeah, later then. Go straight home.

00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.800
<i>He always treats me like a child.</i>

00:03:51.820 --> 00:03:55.590
<i>But he really is a monster.</i>

00:03:55.590 --> 00:03:58.480
<i>There are some differences between the Evo 5 and Evo 6,</i>

00:03:58.480 --> 00:04:02.010
<i>but basically they have the same
specifications for both engine and suspension.</i>

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:08.560
<i>Yet, even when we went into the corner at
the same time, he still went faster than me.</i>

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:15.240
<i>Maybe if my brother didn't have to run our current business,</i>

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:17.740
<i>and had instead opened his own professional tuning shop,</i>

00:04:18.490 --> 00:04:22.910
<i>he would have definitely been the best tuner in Osaka by now.</i>

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:31.080
<i>You took out a Porsche's exhaust manifold,</i>

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:33.840
<i>does that mean the car of your guest
who's coming from Tokyo is...</i>

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.960
<i>Yes, it's a Porsche, 911 Turbo.</i>

00:04:50.970 --> 00:04:52.050
What's wrong?

00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:55.690
When we joined the beltway, a car that stopped at the side...

00:04:56.220 --> 00:04:59.150
seems to be chasing us after seeing our car.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:01.340
You mean, he's been waiting for us?

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.130
Seems like it. He's chasing us with great speed.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:07.340
What type of car is it?

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:08.830
It's a Lan Evo.

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:16.050
Oh I see, this is what he was waiting for.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:22.880
What shall we do?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:26.140
You can do as you please.

00:05:38.860 --> 00:05:42.280
Hey, hey, seems like you're driving extraordinarily fast!

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.570
If I'm not careful, I'll be beaten by you.

00:05:52.290 --> 00:05:56.300
It's not just fast, it's far from the level of Maki.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:01.590
Oh, he's good.

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:05.560
He's fast. But he seems like he's only using 80% of its capacity.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:08.760
He's just being considerate to strangers
who are not familiar with the road.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:20.280
<i>They're the real deal. They're definitely guests of Shige-san.</i>

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:29.160
He slowed down and signaled for a turn.
Seems like he's asking us to follow...

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:33.500
Never mind, just follow. Looks like it'll be interesting.

00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:36.500
But, our purpose tonight was to...

00:06:38.250 --> 00:06:40.710
Who knows, he might just lead us there...

00:06:47.960 --> 00:06:51.270
Shige-san, I picked up your guests.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:52.970
Kitami-san!

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.860
Hi, Shige. It's already been 10 years or should I say more...

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.730
I see you've become an old man too, right?

00:07:02.610 --> 00:07:04.950
The things we did back then...

00:07:07.210 --> 00:07:10.960
Hey Eiji, there's no more beer. Go to the
convenience store and buy some more.

00:07:10.960 --> 00:07:15.750
Uncle, you're drinking too much, you alone finished them all.

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:19.960
You fool, tonight we'll drink until morning, right Kitami-san?

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:22.210
You never change.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:27.720
Porsche... the size is just right, isn't it?

00:07:29.420 --> 00:07:33.000
If I'm not mistaken, the total length is 4250mm,

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:35.730
and its wheelbase is 2270mm, right?

00:07:36.130 --> 00:07:37.040
Yeah.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.340
It's said that it's neither too large or too short,

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:42.780
and is the best suitable size for controlling.

00:07:42.780 --> 00:07:45.200
And the Lan Evo also has about the same size, right?

00:07:45.200 --> 00:07:49.700
Nope, it's 4350mm, 10cm longer.

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:52.500
Its wheelbase is longer too.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:55.910
If we end up racing, this difference of
10cm will affect the outcome, right?

00:07:56.360 --> 00:08:01.960
Just because of that 10cm, nobody can match the speed of this car.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:05.180
<i>That's right Kitami-san,</i>

00:08:05.180 --> 00:08:09.440
<i>this guy who was working in Tokyo came back
here, and was saying something interesting...</i>

00:08:09.440 --> 00:08:15.190
He said that in Tokyo, there's a rumor that there's
a first generation Z which is faster than a GT-R.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:18.200
<i>What nonsense.</i>

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:20.200
I told that fool that's rubbish.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:21.440
There is.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:24.650
Z?! Faster than a GT-R?

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:28.110
It's running and you know it well too.

00:08:28.110 --> 00:08:31.150
What the? It can't be!

00:08:31.790 --> 00:08:35.280
L28 Custom 3.1 Twin Turbo.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:39.420
Still running with 600 horsepower, it's that same S30Z.

00:08:39.960 --> 00:08:43.170
Impossible... that Devil Z...

00:08:43.510 --> 00:08:45.090
Devil Z?

00:08:46.890 --> 00:08:52.140
Shige, the reason I came all the way to Osaka to
see you, is for something related to that Z.

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:57.850
For this Porsche, BlackBird, I want that muffler that you made.

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.150
That's impossible...

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:05.650
No, it's not impossible. If it's you,
it should be done in just 2-3 days, right?

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:07.200
But...

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.110
Why don't you make it, Shige-san?

00:09:09.650 --> 00:09:15.930
This fearful foolish fellow really wants your muffler.

00:09:15.930 --> 00:09:18.830
While waiting, I'll entertain them.

00:09:20.160 --> 00:09:22.190
I knew immediately at first glance.

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:26.260
If this person has Shige-san's muffler, he'll be formidable.

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.470
That Devil Z will surely give up too.

00:09:40.910 --> 00:09:44.650
It's me. Are our guests awake?

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:47.150
Yes, they're having breakfast.

00:09:48.710 --> 00:09:53.160
Got it, I'll tell Maki not to skip his class.

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.160
Later.

00:09:55.400 --> 00:09:58.800
Brother's worrying shames mother's.

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:04.840
His wife is too good for a crazy driver.

00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:07.680
No way, she's my mother.

00:10:07.680 --> 00:10:09.300
Your mother?

00:10:09.300 --> 00:10:12.390
Brother's father and my mother got married.

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:16.390
At that time, my mother was 22 years
old and I was still 3 years old...

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:20.750
So with an age difference of 5-6 years,
she became your brother's step-mother...

00:10:20.750 --> 00:10:21.850
It's complicated.

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:26.850
Whether it's complicated or being a step-brother,
no other brother is better than him.

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:32.300
Oh, this is something great.

00:10:32.300 --> 00:10:35.320
Everything about the cars, he handles by himself.

00:10:39.370 --> 00:10:42.830
Well-used snap-on and welding tools...

00:10:43.450 --> 00:10:46.380
there's even a small milling machine...

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:51.040
That small room over there is an engine room, huh... that's amazing.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:53.880
An unskilled professional will run
away with his tail between his legs.

00:10:54.340 --> 00:10:56.600
Even self-made FRB parts...

00:10:57.260 --> 00:10:59.600
Seems like it's become troublesome.

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:01.350
Brother.

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:05.350
I received an invitation from K Racing, tonight at the Beltway.

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:10.860
They called and asked me to show up, as they
will bring their flagship 600 horsepower car.

00:11:10.860 --> 00:11:13.820
Ah, the S1 from the other day?

00:11:13.820 --> 00:11:18.740
Yeah. Because you agitated them too
much, they could not wait any longer.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:22.040
They said their R34 will be driven by an ex-N1 racer.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:24.040
Great, I'll do it then!

00:11:24.670 --> 00:11:26.190
No, I'll be their opponent.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.800
Shima-san, why don't you drive Maki's Evo?

00:11:30.860 --> 00:11:32.010
W-Why?

00:11:32.920 --> 00:11:36.510
You should sit next to him and observe. You'll learn a lot.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:45.930
I'll be going first then.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:52.350
It's you...

00:11:52.350 --> 00:11:54.530
What do you mean "It's you..."?

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:57.550
And I was just about to give you some very valuable information.

00:11:57.550 --> 00:11:58.450
Information?

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:02.700
Since you gave me such a reaction,
I don't feel like giving it to you for free.

00:12:05.430 --> 00:12:07.420
So, what's this "information"?

00:12:08.250 --> 00:12:10.520
You think a cup of coffee is enough?

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:11.930
Then what do you want?

00:12:12.540 --> 00:12:17.170
Wangan on Akio-kun's Z, in the passenger seat. I'm free tomorrow...

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.440
I get it, I get it, ok.

00:12:19.860 --> 00:12:21.000
Great!

00:12:21.000 --> 00:12:25.520
Well, it seems that BlackBird is now in Osaka with Kitami-san.

00:12:25.520 --> 00:12:27.400
Osaka? What for?

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:30.430
Something like getting a muffler made or some sort.

00:12:30.430 --> 00:12:32.570
This information came from boss Yamamoto.

00:12:32.570 --> 00:12:35.450
The boss heard this from Tominaga-san.

00:12:35.450 --> 00:12:41.400
He brought the car all the way there,
is that muffler really that great?

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:51.620
Tachometer show Rev 1 at 7000rpm, how high can it go?

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:51.920
<i>Tachometer, an instrument that measures the rotation speed of a motor.</i>

00:12:52.050 --> 00:12:53.680
Up to 8000rpm.

00:12:54.590 --> 00:12:58.180
It's been more than 20 years since I first met Shige.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:00.690
Back then it was called Aoyama 04.

00:13:01.150 --> 00:13:04.420
At first, it was just 5-6 cars playing around...

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:09.690
but after that, various modified car started
gathering at Aoyama on Saturday midnights.

00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:15.400
Rumors spread, there were some people
who came from afar, like Shige from Osaka.

00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:21.660
It was a time when we'd never expect
that tuning could become a business.

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:28.160
After that there's the Tohmei Race, Yatabe
Max Speed Shutokou and then Wangan...

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:34.130
The energy generated at that time started to
seek out its own place and move towards it.

00:13:45.850 --> 00:13:47.730
It's here, the R34 from K Racing!

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.280
Why did you give way?

00:13:52.280 --> 00:13:57.980
Because I'm racing at an unfamiliar place with a unfamiliar car,
and that I don't fully understand this car as well.

00:14:01.490 --> 00:14:04.200
It's here, it's here! Sticking to my car right at the start.

00:14:06.950 --> 00:14:09.960
Hey, you think I'd simply let you get in front?

00:14:22.860 --> 00:14:24.520
If I'm not careful, I'll be taken down.

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:26.350
As expected, a campaign-sponsored car is fast.

00:14:36.810 --> 00:14:39.940
I'm getting to know how to drive this car.

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:49.500
<i>As expected of him, observe well from beside
him, Maki, what true skill and true speed is.</i>

00:14:52.490 --> 00:14:54.500
<i>Burn it into your eyes.</i>

00:14:58.960 --> 00:15:00.960
He turned on his hazard lights!

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:02.960
K Racing is going to give up.

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:06.680
<i>The other side is also a professional racer, he's not stupid.</i>

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:11.440
<i>He knows the difference in level and is
not going to continue a losing battle.</i>

00:15:11.850 --> 00:15:13.480
<i>You understand, right Maki?</i>

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.980
<i>There's no point putting so much thought into theory.</i>

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:18.690
<i>Only what your eyes see means everything.</i>

00:15:19.990 --> 00:15:23.930
<i>Nice, Shige. A muffler should prioritize efficiency,</i>

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:26.410
<i>but it undeniably sounds good.</i>

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:30.450
<i>I cannot control my excitement, I'll get that muffler.</i>

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.120
Shige-san.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:48.640
I brought you some food.

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:51.140
Ah, thanks, Eiji.

00:15:53.390 --> 00:15:58.900
It's been already 10 years since your
dad died leaving his debt unpaid, right?

00:15:58.900 --> 00:16:00.970
You've worked really hard.

00:16:00.970 --> 00:16:05.790
The delinquent who didn't finish high
school properly suddenly became a boss.

00:16:05.790 --> 00:16:09.330
But you still worked very hard from morning to night without rest,

00:16:09.330 --> 00:16:14.410
settled all his debt and sent your step-brother
to university. What a great person!

00:16:14.410 --> 00:16:17.910
What are you saying now? What are you
getting at, praising me all of a sudden?

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:21.430
But, Eiji, are you satisfied with this?

00:16:21.800 --> 00:16:22.420
Huh?

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:24.890
Is this really alright with you?

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:28.190
I've always thought you wanted to live alongside your car.

00:16:28.190 --> 00:16:31.850
You drive on the beltway and do stuff
like embarrassing other tuners,

00:16:31.850 --> 00:16:34.430
how much longer are you going to lie to yourself?

00:16:34.430 --> 00:16:37.940
You think too much, I'm not really...

00:16:37.940 --> 00:16:40.940
It's a good opportunity, go to Tokyo.

00:16:41.510 --> 00:16:43.210
W-What are you saying?!

00:16:43.210 --> 00:16:46.820
Most people cannot live a life without regret, right?

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:49.700
Like me, it's always an on parade of regrets.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:56.100
I had regrets, but I am satisfied with my life.

00:16:56.100 --> 00:16:59.200
Although I've been making straight
mufflers at the motorcycle factory nearby,

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:05.050
but even now there are still people who
want my mufflers. I'm really happy.

00:17:05.050 --> 00:17:07.470
That's right, I understand.

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:11.720
I'm not saying you should give up everything and become a tuner,

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:16.930
but are you satisfied remaining a half-ass driver in this town?

00:17:17.670 --> 00:17:21.690
Go to Tokyo and drive with true drivers at Shutokou Area.

00:17:25.330 --> 00:17:26.750
That's unusual.

00:17:26.750 --> 00:17:28.570
I'm just passing by.

00:17:28.570 --> 00:17:30.450
Hey, Rikako, tea please.

00:17:34.550 --> 00:17:36.700
Sometimes, she helps me.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:40.150
She's like her mother, even though
she's a woman, she's good at driving.

00:17:42.100 --> 00:17:45.420
I see, Kitami went to see Shige...

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:50.720
I remember the old days, all looking dirty
and hanging around Tokyo back then.

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:53.180
Yeah, we even slept in the car.

00:17:53.860 --> 00:17:58.680
I look forward to seeing the BlackBird
with the muffler made by Shige.

00:18:01.100 --> 00:18:04.030
How's my brother's car, Tatsuya-san?

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:09.420
It's good. The rear has traction and
the front pulls, the setting is superb.

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:12.700
Right?! Recently, he's been especially
particular about the suspension.

00:18:14.860 --> 00:18:17.660
Please, floor the accelerator more, Tatsuya-san!

00:18:21.720 --> 00:18:23.160
What are you thinking?

00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:25.680
Oh, nothing much.

00:18:25.680 --> 00:18:28.880
About BlackBird, right? It's disturbing you after all?

00:18:30.930 --> 00:18:35.440
Boring. Even when I finally got to ride Z...

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:46.700
Yes, I'll leave in 30 minutes, thanks.

00:18:46.700 --> 00:18:48.820
You look busy, boss.

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:52.160
If compared to last time, it's become much easier now.

00:18:53.290 --> 00:18:55.910
Maki has become completely attached to Shima-san.

00:18:55.910 --> 00:19:01.410
Last night too, he borrowed my Evo 5 and
they've been driving together the whole time.

00:19:02.400 --> 00:19:04.410
We'll go back to Tokyo tonight.

00:19:04.410 --> 00:19:07.510
I see.

00:19:07.510 --> 00:19:10.090
Shige's muffler will be ready tonight,

00:19:10.090 --> 00:19:13.680
after which we'll briefly check in on the
Beltway and then head back to Tokyo.

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:16.230
Then we'll be missing you.

00:19:16.230 --> 00:19:21.390
But Tokyo is surprisingly quite near,
maybe we may come visit you one day.

00:19:21.390 --> 00:19:22.640
It may be impossible.

00:19:23.810 --> 00:19:26.360
Just Shige alone, we haven't met again for more than 10 years.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.650
You have your own way of living...

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:34.410
and we have our own way of living in Tokyo.

00:19:35.220 --> 00:19:37.870
Unexpectedly, that day may never come.

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:41.750
Thank you so much for your kindness.

00:19:41.750 --> 00:19:44.360
No. it's nothing.

00:19:44.360 --> 00:19:46.170
See you then. Thanks a lot.

00:19:47.440 --> 00:19:53.890
Are you the person who built the Devil Z that's
empowered with 600 horsepower, Kitami-san?

00:19:54.380 --> 00:19:55.930
That was quite a long time ago.

00:19:55.930 --> 00:19:58.390
The owner has changed a few times,

00:19:58.390 --> 00:20:00.890
and now a young man, Akio, is driving it.

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:03.600
He's about the same age as your younger brother.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.610
<i>Neither stepping, nor releasing the accelerator.</i>

00:20:12.030 --> 00:20:16.570
<i>This delicate level cannot be maintained. This muffler is unstable.</i>

00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.610
<i>The power certainly has been reduced.</i>

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:25.250
<i>But, what is this feeling of elevation?</i>

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.420
<i>It was the same for that Evo 5.</i>

00:20:27.420 --> 00:20:31.390
<i>The sound... the sound comes flying directly into my body.</i>

00:20:32.820 --> 00:20:35.840
<i>Does changing just one muffler make such a big difference?</i>

00:20:37.800 --> 00:20:39.720
I'm counting on you, drive safely.

00:20:41.850 --> 00:20:43.390
Just left for Tokyo?

00:20:43.930 --> 00:20:45.480
Yes, where's Maki?

00:20:46.240 --> 00:20:50.110
He said, on his way back from sending Kitami-san
and Shima-san off, he'll be driving on the beltway.

00:20:50.110 --> 00:20:53.400
I'm afraid he'll go and follow them straight to Tokyo.

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:57.610
The person who really wants to follow
them to Tokyo is you, right Eiji-san?

00:20:58.320 --> 00:20:59.860
No such thing!

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:05.370
Say, Eiji-san, shall we close down our company?

00:21:06.020 --> 00:21:07.130
What are you saying?

00:21:08.040 --> 00:21:11.800
My husband did whatever he like while he was still alive,

00:21:11.800 --> 00:21:17.090
accumulated debt and then died, after
which the debt became your burden, Eiji-san.

00:21:17.090 --> 00:21:22.640
Maki and I are a burden to you ever
since then, that I understand very well.

00:21:22.640 --> 00:21:23.930
No, I...

00:21:23.930 --> 00:21:28.350
You have already taken care of us even on his behalf, Eiji-san.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:32.840
If we close down our company, and sell our land and buildings,

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:36.320
even after we settle the debt, we still have balance.

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:38.130
You can go to Tokyo with that money.

00:21:38.130 --> 00:21:38.780
Eriko-san...

00:21:39.720 --> 00:21:44.410
I can work anywhere and Maki also can
go to university while working part-time.

00:21:45.550 --> 00:21:49.210
I'm sorry, we should actually have done this earlier.

00:21:51.620 --> 00:21:53.630
It's not too late at all.

00:21:54.210 --> 00:21:57.660
Chase your dream, Eiji-san!

00:21:57.660 --> 00:22:02.130
Maki will also understand. Not only that, he'll be rather happy.

00:22:04.420 --> 00:22:09.180
Eiji! If you don't do it now, you'll regret it for the rest of your life.

00:22:09.620 --> 00:22:15.150
I also thought the same way, I delivered Make when
I was 18 years old and got married with your father.

00:22:15.850 --> 00:22:19.090
Although I suffered, I think it was right.

00:22:19.090 --> 00:22:21.700
It's much better than doing nothing.

00:22:24.830 --> 00:22:29.710
Three months... for three months, can
you run the company without me?

00:22:30.410 --> 00:22:32.500
I will settle everything and return by then.

00:22:32.500 --> 00:22:36.120
Return? It's alright, we'll just close down...

00:22:36.120 --> 00:22:37.710
I'll return, after three months!

00:22:38.710 --> 00:22:42.840
All this time, I have been waiting to go
to Tokyo and find some challenges.

00:22:42.840 --> 00:22:48.680
But I couldn't. It's not because of you, Eriko-san nor Maki.

00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:52.860
Whatever it is, I was comfortable here,

00:22:52.860 --> 00:22:58.690
and even though I go to Tokyo, I might just end
up in shame. In the end, it's just because of this.

00:22:59.390 --> 00:23:02.490
I'm not thinking of becoming a professional drive anymore.

00:23:02.490 --> 00:23:05.010
If you're gonna call me something, call me a loser.

00:23:05.010 --> 00:23:08.940
I'll get a straight answer of whether I'm a loser or not.

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:12.760
In Tokyo, the Tokyo which I've been waiting to go all this time...
